From 14713d03831e3209a9d2891d78c71ea4fc2921f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:09:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm, estuary, language: say where Dolby Vision
 Low-Latency maps an HDR10+ picture by its tone curve

The row "RPU" of the Dolby Vision page of the player information said "L1 from
HDR10+ statistics, no tone curve" for every picture of HDR10+ sent as Dolby
Vision. In Low-Latency, a picture that the bridge mapped by the tone curve of
its HDR10+ metadata now shows "L1 from HDR10+, its tone curve applied"
(hades.dv.origin "hdr10pluscurve", of the frame presented), in the four
languages, on Estuary's page and on the generated one of Hades.

The help of "Play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision" said that the studio's tone
curve does not carry over; it now says that in Dolby Vision Low-Latency (game
mode), where Hades adapts each picture to the TV itself, the curve is applied.
